e] [17592186361813 1100 "Find an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}-14 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -20 & 17 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361813 1113 #uuid "0e67636c-732e-5418-86ed-bc13bbb0d106" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361813 1145 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -20 & 17 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -20 & 15 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-16{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -20{x}_{1}+15{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 12 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -20 & 15 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{5}{4}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 12 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-16 & 12 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this in the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{2}=4,$ we get the eigenvector\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361815 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361816 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361817 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361818 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361819 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1041 "selection" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361818 13194139535696 true] [17592186361814 1110 #uuid "19d39da7-dc72-5459-a5ed-520ae68960af" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361815 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361815 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361815 1111 #uuid "db13efdc-4937-54a0-b367-0747d4055a5a" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361816 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361816 1111 #uuid "a9c2f0d4-d36c-5368-a963-bb75d34e33bc" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361817 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361817 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361817 1111 #uuid "31d78fc4-3c30-5eef-89da-2bdd749920b6" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361818 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361818 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361818 1111 #uuid "daa92a92-9a4f-5e04-8aa4-4b9561a7c92d" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361819 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361819 1111 #uuid "76870c09-96be-5b0f-ac8c-dc372736434f" 1319