{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the augmented matrix $M$ is already in its row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{4}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{5}{4}{x}_{3})-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5{x}_{3}-3{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{3}=4,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{8}{4}=2.$" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361822 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361823 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361824 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361825 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361826 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1041 "selection" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361822 13194139535696 true] [17592186361821 1110 #uuid "02516065-d4f5-5816-ae15-b7fd983b8424" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361822 1034 "2" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true] [17592186361822 1111 #uuid "d9d109c1-c769-5aac-b1a5-c1377741d0b5" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361823 1034 "\\frac{8}{5}" 13194139535696 true] [17592186361823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535696 true